    "description": "Noe Valley two-unit building on the market for the first time in over 45 years!    When the owner bought it, it was their foot into San Francisco.  Over the years, this substantial building has been thoughtfully improved, remodeled, maintained and enjoyed.    The building sits on a deep lot and has a large, lush garden with access to the street, which both units share. The interior has Victorian detail, wood floors and generous rooms.  There is a large garage with extra storage.    236 27th, the upper, two bedroom, two bath flat, was the owner's home for many years and upgraded to their taste.  It is light with large windows, tall ceilings and skylights, with a large kitchen, formal dining room and in-unit laundry.  The home is currently vacant.    236B 27th, the lower, two bedroom, one bath flat is a beautifully cared for tenant occupied unit.    The property is great opportunity as an investment, or owner occupier to get your piece of the San Francisco pie.  The home is conveniently located near MUNI, neighborhood shopping, tech  buses and freeways."
  },
